PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772734904
OL,1,V7w3s7s35B                         G5/19
OL,2,V55555555CREFORMISTS AHEAD IN
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CSOVIET ELECTIONS
OL,5, Candidates backing sweeping reform in
OL,6, the Soviet Union are far ahead of
OL,7, orthodox Communists as returns trickle
OL,8, in from elections in three republics.
OL,10, Maverick politician Boris Yeltsin took
OL,11, 72% of the vote in the Urals city of
OL,12, Sverdlovsk to win a seat in the Russian
OL,13, parliament.
OL,15, President Gorbachev says the elections
OL,16, there and in Byelorussia and the
OL,17, Ukraine are vital for perestroika.
OL,19, Elsewhere, TV presenters, journalists,
OL,20, actors and economists were elected but
OL,21, there will be run-offs for many seats.
OL,23,F]DFrom 05-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772734904
OL,1,V7w3s7s35E                         G6/19
OL,2,V55555555CNHS: 70% OPPOSE
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CCHANGES, SAYS BMA
OL,4,         C
OL,5, More than seven out of 10 voters are
OL,6, against the Government's health
OL,7, reforms, says a survey commissioned by
OL,8, the British Medical Association.
OL,10, Seventy per cent dislike the idea of
OL,11, their GPs being limited in their
OL,12, decisions by a financial budget.
OL,14, A huge 77% of Tory voters and 70% of
OL,15, the entire sample thought any changes
OL,16, should be tested first in a pilot area
OL,17, before being implemented nationally.
OL,19, Overall, Conservative voters were
OL,20, evenly divided on the issues raised by
OL,21, the NHS and Community Care Bill.
OL,23,F]DFrom 05-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49607
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772734904
OL,1,V7w3s7s35B                         G7/19
OL,2,V55555555CISRAEL DEFIES USA
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5COVER SOVIET JEWS
OL,4,         C
OL,5, Israel is defying her closest ally, the
OL,6, United States, and calling for the
OL,7, settling of as many Soviet Jewish
OL,8, immigrants as possible in Jerusalem.
OL,10, Prime Minister Yitzhak Shamir's remarks
OL,11, follow President Bush's demand for a
OL,12, halt to their settlement in the Arab,
OL,13, eastern part seized by Israel in 1967.
OL,15, Jerusalem is at the centre of the
OL,16, Israeli-Palestinian conflict, with each
OL,17, side claiming it for its capital.
OL,19, Israel is wrangling over US proposals
OL,20, to let West Bank Palestinians who live
OL,21, in E Jerusalem join Cairo peace talks.
OL,23,F]DFrom 05-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49608
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772734904
OL,1,V7w3s7s35                          G8/19
OL,2,V55555555CBANK FAILS TO HALT
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CSTERLING'S SLIDE
OL,5, The Bank of England bought pounds to
OL,6, shore up sterling but it failed to halt
OL,7, a slide, prompted by fears over the
OL,8, Government's poor ratings in the polls.
OL,10, After an early rally it dipped more
OL,11, than a cent against the dollar and four
OL,12, pfennigs against the West German mark.
OL,14, Fears that inflation could hit 9% have
OL,15, raised the possibility of another rise
OL,16, in interest rates, even though they are
OL,17, failing to dampen demand for credit.
OL,19, Credit card companies and other lenders
OL,20, advanced #3.95bn in January compared to
OL,21, #3.38bn in December, denting Chancellor
OL,22, John Major's hopes of curbing borrowing
OL,23,F]DFrom 05-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49609
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772734904
OL,1,V7w3s7s35B                         G9/19
OL,2,V55555555CPATTEN ACTS TO
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CCLEAN UP NORTH SEA
OL,5, Britain is to ban the discharge of raw
OL,6, sewage from coastal towns by the end of
OL,7, 1998, Environment Secretary Chris
OL,8, Patten has announced.
OL,10, And the incineration of waste at sea
OL,11, will be banned by the end of this year.
OL,13, He told a London press conference that
OL,14, the action demonstrated Britain's
OL,15, commitment to "improving the quality of
OL,16, the North Sea and our coastal waters."
OL,18, Mr Patten announced the measures on the
OL,19, eve of the third North Sea ministers'
OL,20, conference in The Hague.
OL,23,F]DFrom 05-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
